.!	MAN-MKMETHOD.RI   Man page for OOC Method Maker             Aug 89, bjw
.!
.!
.!
.! --------------
.!
.vs progname "mkmethod"
.vs product "Object Oriented C"
.vs list  "method selector code list"
.!
.! --------------
.!
.source manual.rinc
.!
.! --------------
.!
.header /${progname}(OOPS)//${vers}/
.footer /%//Page #/
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Name
${progname} - Maintains ${list}.
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Syntax
.bold
${progname}
[-uv] method_name..
.br
.bold
${progname}
-q method__name [-q method__name]..
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Description
.!
.program ${progname}
allows the user to update the ${list},
or to query to see if a method already exists.
Status information is sent to stdout.
The first form adds methods to the ${list} if they don't
exist there already.
The second form just queries the position of the named method.
The text names are used by the substrate routines
in printing error messages.
The methods include file is only updated if new methods are added.
.sp
.!
When used to add methods, the method name contains the selectors.
Colons (_:) denote where parameters are placed, ie, "at:put:".
The case of the selector names is important;
spaces seperate methods on the command line.
If the methods aren't duplicates, they will be added to the end
of the ${list}.
The method include file is only rewritten when methods are added.
Updating can be forced by the
.filename -u
flag.
You should do this after a deletion to remove the ``hole''.
.sp
.!
The second form allows the user to query the ${list} to see
if a method exists.
The include file is not updated in this mode.
If the method is found, it's position is printed out.
If the method can't be located, a message stating this is printed.
.sp
.!
If you must delete methods, for instance they were entered misspelled,
then an editor can be used to remove the offending method.
Only the string name need to removed.
Once done, run
.program ${progname}_,
with the
.filename -u
option, and the include file will be rebuilt.
You must now recompile all the classes in the system,
to make sure no one uses that method.
The method selectors are constants
that have already been compiled into the object code,
and you may have caused value to change.
Failure to recompile could damage your system and/or
cause the application to fail.
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Files
ooc(OOPS).
.br
ooc:include/methods.h
.br
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Example
Here are a few invokation samples to ponder.
Output of the program is omitted for brevity sake.
.!
.opencode
>>> mkmethod error:vaDcl:
>>> mkmethod at: at:put: atChar: atChar:put:
>>> mkmethod -q at:put:
.closecode
.!
.! +++++++++++++++++++++++++
.!
.section Bugs
This program needs a silence mode so automated tools can query
the ${list} for the user.
.!
.!
.!   *** EOJ
